          "settings": {
            "eyebrow": "Connected vehicle technology",
            "title": "What Is a 4G LTE Dash Cam?",
            "introduction": "<h3>What Is a 4G LTE Dash Cam?</h3><p>A 4G LTE dash cam is a connected vehicle camera that uses a cellular network to support remote features beyond the local WiFi connection found on many standard dash cams.</p><p>Depending on the camera, 4G connectivity may enable remote vehicle monitoring, remote access, GPS tracking, parking notifications, or other connected services while you are away from the vehicle.</p><p>This makes a 4G dash cam particularly useful for drivers who want to stay connected to their vehicle even when they are not sitting inside it.</p>",
            "benefits": "<h3>Why Choose a 4G Dash Cam?</h3><p>The biggest advantage of a 4G dash cam is connectivity beyond the vehicle. With a traditional WiFi dash cam, your smartphone generally needs to be near the camera to establish a direct WiFi connection. A 4G LTE dash cam can use cellular connectivity to support compatible remote features over a much greater distance.</p><p>This can make 4G dash cams useful for:</p><ul><li>Remote vehicle monitoring</li><li>Parking protection</li><li>GPS vehicle tracking</li><li>Checking on a parked vehicle</li><li>Business and commercial vehicles</li><li>Drivers who frequently leave their vehicles parked for extended periods</li></ul>",
